  "notes": "Per the 2026-2027 Texas A&M University undergraduate catalog: Marine Engineering Technology — License Option (BS). Prerequisites are not listed in the catalog's plan of study grid; consult course descriptions.\nCatalog footnotes:\n[grid1 fn1] Indicates license courses leading to a USCG/STCW license endorsement or sea time or workshops skills credit accrual which require a minimum grade of C (70%) or better to earn the endorsement or workshop skills accrual. Cadets will be required to repeat the course until they earn a grade of C (70%) or better. Failure to meet this requirement will prevent the student from continuing any sequence in which the course is a prerequisite.\n[grid1 fn2] Students are required to earn a grade of C or better in MATH 151 , MATH 152 , PHYS 206 , PHYS 207 , PHYS 226 , PHYS 227 , MARE 202 , MARE 205 , MARE 206 , MARE 207 , and MARE 209 . Failure to meet this requirement will prevent the student from continuing any sequence in which the course is a prerequisite.\n[grid1 fn3] Indicates required courses in the Marine Engineering Technology License Option major. These courses will be used to compute the major GPA.\n[grid1 fn4] Designated Writing intensive course.\n[grid1 fn5] Technical electives may be any course with the following prefixes: CSCE, MARE, MART, OCEN, MATH, PHYS, MARS, or OCNG at the 300 or 400 level in consultation with the student's advisor.",
